IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-part1-general`

-- Tests for Part 1 and Part 1A. Every expected value is written from the text (the line is cited),
-- never copied from what the module printed.

§ `Part 1`

§§ `Dates the text fixes`

-- Line 4: "Made 9th February 2015".
#ASSERT `the date the Regulations were made` EQUALS Date 9 2 2015
-- Lines 5 and 14: "Coming into force 6th April 2016".
#ASSERT `the date the Regulations come into force` EQUALS Date 6 4 2016

§§ `Regulation 1(3): pensionable age before 6 April 2016`

-- Line 15: the Regulations (except Part 5) do not apply to a person who reaches pensionable age before 6th April 2016.
-- The day before 6 April 2016 is before it; 6 April 2016 itself is not.
#ASSERT `whether Parts 1 to 4 and 6 to 8 apply to a person who reaches pensionable age on` (Date 5 4 2016) EQUALS `these Regulations do not apply to the person, who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016`
#ASSERT `whether Parts 1 to 4 and 6 to 8 apply to a person who reaches pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2016) EQUALS `these Regulations apply to the person`
#ASSERT `whether Parts 1 to 4 and 6 to 8 apply to a person who reaches pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS `these Regulations apply to the person`
#ASSERT `whether Parts 1 to 4 and 6 to 8 apply to a person who reaches pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 1990) EQUALS `these Regulations do not apply to the person, who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016`

§§ `Regulation 1(5): married to a third person`

`a married couple` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
    `how they are joined` IS `married to each other`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS FALSE

`a married couple where one is also married to a third person` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
    `how they are joined` IS `married to each other`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS TRUE

`civil partners` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
    `how they are joined` IS `civil partners of each other`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS FALSE

`civil partners where one is married to a third person` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
    `how they are joined` IS `civil partners of each other`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS TRUE

`two unrelated people` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
    `how they are joined` IS `not married to each other and not civil partners`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS FALSE

-- Line 22: two people are treated as if they are not married to each other in relation to times
-- when either of them is married to a third person.
#ASSERT `the two people are treated as married to each other` `a married couple`
#ASSERT NOT (`the two people are treated as married to each other` `a married couple where one is also married to a third person`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the two people are treated as married to each other` `civil partners`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the two people are treated as married to each other` `two unrelated people`)
-- Only the marriage is taken away; civil partners stay civil partners.
#ASSERT `the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners of each other` `a married couple`
#ASSERT NOT (`the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners of each other` `a married couple where one is also married to a third person`)
#ASSERT `the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners of each other` `civil partners`
#ASSERT `the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners of each other` `civil partners where one is married to a third person`
#ASSERT NOT (`the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners of each other` `two unrelated people`)

§§ `A counting convention: a period of months starting on a day (fork F7)`

#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `months starting on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 31 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `months starting on` (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS Date 14 2 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `months starting on` (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `months starting on` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 `months starting on` (Date 1 12 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 `months starting on` (Date 30 11 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 12 `months starting on` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 31 12 2026

§ `Part 1A`

-- Line 25: the full rate of the state pension is £241.30 per week.
#ASSERT `the full rate of the state pension, in pounds per week` EQUALS 241.30
